tide  but as winter approaches  climbing numbers of infections there and  in other parts of the continent have  found doubts on whether at least some  measures  might have to be reintroduced so  long story short i'm guessing  that life hasn't really returned to to  normal anywhere but as i said at the  start  i think that's become a pretty relative  term  and before we go opposition to  coronavirus mandates has been growing in  parts of the u.s like in new york city  where vaccine mandate opponents held a  nighttime demonstration on staten island  the protest came after about 9 000 of  the city's 300 000 municipal workers  were put on unpaid leave for refusing to  comply with a new rule requiring them to  get vaccinated against covet 19.  thousands of city firefighters called in  sick in an apparent protest over the  requirement the mayor says  there have been no disruptions to city  services  that's our show thanks for watching  [Music]
 

